Recommend 7 flagship initiatives sequenced across Q1–Q6 (priority = fast NRR impact then product differentiation scale): 
1) ICP & portfolio rationalization + bespoke packaging for top 2 segments — Owner: Head of GTM; Phase Q1–Q2; KPIs: % ARR in prioritized segments, win rate ↑, ACV ↑; 
2) Customer Success “NRR Lift” program (playbooks + predictive health & expansion motions) — Owner: VP Customer Success; Phase Q1–Q4; KPIs: NRR +8–10 pts in core segments, renewal rate, expansion ARR; 
3) Pricing & term simplification (value‑based tiers, multi‑year incentives) — Owner: VP Commercial/Finance; Phase Q1–Q3; KPIs: ACV uplift, % multi‑year contracts, gross margin delta; 
4) Scalable mid‑market channel (self‑serve + inside sales automation) — Owner: VP Growth; Phase Q1–Q4; KPIs: CAC payback, conversion, new ARR sourced. 
5) AI‑assisted workflow MVP (2 high‑value workflows) — Owner: Head of Product/CTO; Phase Q2–Q4 (MVP) → Q5 scale; KPIs: adoption rate, feature-driven expansion lift, time‑to‑value reduction; 
6) Three strategic deep integrations + partner GTM — Owner: Head of Partnerships/CTO; Phase Q2–Q6; KPIs: integration‑sourced ARR, win rate with integrations, integration usage; 
7) NPS & Advocacy system (sprints + reference program) — Owner: Head of CS & Marketing; Phase Q1–Q3; KPIs: NPS Δ, # referenceable customers, referral pipeline. 
Governance/guardrails: one clear owner per initiative, quarterly milestones and 2–3 KPIs, limit to three concurrent cross‑functional squads in any quarter, and escalate monthly to the CEO/CSO with a Board pressure‑test each quarter. 
If this prioritization looks right, confirm owners and we’ll map detailed quarterly milestones and resource needs for the next leadership sync.
